# Two PRs appending a row to one assumptions table, or an entry to one package's mutgate record, keep both
# on a local merge. A line both add word for word is one line to every reader (#6358); doclint, mutgate and
# premerge fail one ID or mutant key on two different lines, and premerge reads an entry the union brought back
# as changed. GitHub's server-side merge ignores this file (agents merge main locally). A clone that ran
# `tools/record_merge.py --install` merges both files by key instead (info/attributes), so an edited line is not
# kept twice and an identical one is kept once; CI and premerge's replay keep the union.
ASSUMPTIONS.md merge=union
MUTANTS-EQUIVALENT merge=union
